{
  "id": "T18_51_adopt_policy_takes_effect_when_made_and_earlier_endings_stand",
  "family": "T18",
  "rules": [
    "7.7.2",
    "7.7.3",
    "7.6.14",
    "8.4.1",
    "9.5.1",
    "9.5.3",
    "9.5.7",
    "2.4.4",
    "12.19"
  ],
  "description": "Two change stories are governed from the start by the fixture policy. Monday's directive on chg-a establishes a lacquer requirement that is still outstanding on Thursday, so chg-a stays open; Monday's directive on chg-b is closed on Tuesday when its requirement is fulfilled. On Wednesday adoptions of the baseline are recorded for both stories with @effective Thursday 09:00. A Wednesday frame is unchanged: chg-a is open under the fixture policy. From Thursday the baseline governs: chg-a ends at Thursday 09:00, because its baseline ending (the review) already held, with the review as its ending record; chg-b keeps its Tuesday ending under the fixture policy, directive_closed. Neither adoption records any act.",
  "note": "7.7.3: \"It takes effect when it is made, at its context's occurrence time or at `@effective` (8.4.1) ... A period that had ended at or before T, under the policy then governing the unit, keeps that ending. A period open at T (7.6.3) is governed by the newly adopted policy from T ... where that ending already held before T, it ends at T.\" 7.6.14: the ending's time \"is the later of that act's `at` and the instant from which that policy has governed the unit without interruption up to that ending\". README section 5, Periods: `policy_end` \"is the end act of the policy governing the unit when the period ends ... `policy_end` then also carries `policy`, naming that policy (`null` when the baseline governs the period's ending)\". 8.4.1 and 2.4.4 allow @effective on adopt_policy. A `periods` list \"lists the recorded periods whatever the cutoff\" (README section 5), so the Wednesday read already shows the Thursday policy_end while the standing is open.",
